  "why": "Janus head of Tripo task 330872a3 (measured 2026-09-29, work/probe sheets): the side concept (drawn over ortho_left, face looking left) went into the RIGHT slot, so Tripo fitted a face on BOTH sides of the head (-Y: tripo_part_12 from the front concept; +Y: tripo_part_0 from the mirrored side profile) and swept the wings toward -Y. Turning the high-poly 180 deg about Z makes the side-consistent face (tripo_part_0, with a real nose/chin profile) the front and sweeps the wings back as in the side concept; the front-concept face part tripo_part_12 is dropped. The dropped face sat inside a feathered hood of the TORSO part tripo_part_1 (its neck column behind the head, authored y -0.026..0.070, rising to z 0.534 = eye level): that hood stays hollow after the drop (open toward +Y, its inside faces the viewer from behind) and reads from the elevated game camera as a smooth bald dome behind the crest (harpy-h2-bake/1 review, verifier frames 2026-09-29). Profile /2 trims it (repair.trim), closes the torso's neck opening with a closed cap (repair.caps) and covers the cap's upper half with a copy of the head's own back feathers (repair.patches). The back of tripo_part_0 itself is a closed feathered surface. The second ankle band tripo_part_11 (right leg after the turn) is kept because it is structural (see kept_parts_note). Repair of a generation defect, proposal; regeneration with the side view in the LEFT slot is the clean fix (followup)"
 },
